Today, Oakland is one of the most diverse cities in the United States, but some worry that diversity is diluting its black cultural identity. This is an issue affecting cities across the country like Atlanta, Washington, D.C., and Newark, New Jersey. NPR's Shireen Marisol Maragi has our story.

