Everything stopped for a moment at this first Friday to honor Keontae Campbell, an 18-year-old student shot and killed last month. Three-quarters of the murder victims in Oakland are Black, like Keontae. Those two factors, higher rents and crime, are triggers for the nearly 25 percent drop in Oakland's Black population over the last two decades.

